  "worked_solution": "In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(8,5),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{5\\text{\u00a0m/s}-0\\text{\u00a0m/s}}{8\\text{\u00a0s}-0\\text{\u00a0s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{\u00a0m/s}}{8\\text{\u00a0s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the surfer is $\\frac{5}{8}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$",
